after coming home from a long trip a  valley family discovered their apartment  was overgrown with black mold and that  they had a roach infestation eight news  now investigates as the family is now  forced out of their home  latoya barnes her husband dante gilmer  and their three young children were  forced to leave their apartment and  everything they own after the place was  completely infested with black mold this  happened in the central valley at the  university gardens apartments north of  flamingo road and university center  the family says it's not a safe place to  stay as the mold has grown over the  walls and floor and roaches have  infested the entire unit barnes claims  the mold was there before and she asked  the complex to fix it but says they  never did and once they left for a  three-week trip it got out of control we  reached out to the apartment complex in  a statement they said in part westland  university gardens takes all appropriate  actions to provide a safe community and  environment for our residents  maintenance technicians staff and  vendors  they also claim that barnes did not  allow them to enter the apartment  without her there and said when they  told her the unit was no longer livable  she became quote angry and belligerent  she then proceeded to verbally and  physically assault the management staff  end quote the company said it wants to  resolve the issue as soon as possible  barnes had another version of that  confrontation and said she was trying to  keep office staff at a distance during a  heated argument she says she is now  speaking with an attorney for that full  statement and a closer look at this  story head to our website eight newsnow  dot com
 

